WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.340
They're big, they're ugly, and they're coming to get us.

00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:04.780
It's the invasion, of the monster King Crab.

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:11.860
King Crab is the largest crustacean in the world,

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:13.520
And they're heading for Britain.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:18.240
GORDON: Norway has a massive problem

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:20.220
with these huge, giant King Crabs.

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:22.760
They're just breeding, and breeding, and breeding,

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:25.820
reducing the fish stocks, and causing a huge problem.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:29.680
All the King Crab that come to England are frozen,

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:32.140
so I'm now going to catch one, kill one,

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:35.460
and see what it actually tastes like fresh from the sea.

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:41.480
VOICEOVER: Two flights and eight hours later, I land in (INAUDIBLE).

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:44.440
Where I met my local crab hunter, Lars Petter Oy. 
(Sorry if I misspelled your name)

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:47.020
LARS: Welcome.
GORDON: Thank you, I'm very happy to be here.

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:47.800
I've never been this far up.

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:49.600
(WHISPERS) It's f***ing freezing here.
(LAUGHS)

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:52.740
There's only one way to get around in Norwegian Lapland,

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:53.920
And it's not by car...

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:56.040
(ENGINE REVS)

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:07.780
We're heading over the mountains, and down to the frozen fjord,

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:09.440
which is where the crabs hang out.

00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:12.840
GORDON: Woo-hoo!

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:25.620
GORDON: Excellent.

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:28.640
Unbelievable. 
LARS: You feel like a child again.

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:31.380
GORDON: Yeah, that was extraordinary!
LARS: This is Anton.

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:33.980
GORDON: Anton, how are you? Good to see you.

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:36.800
(DRILLING)

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:39.640
50,000 crabs live under this ice,

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:42.740
and if we want to catch one, we're going to have to dive down beneath it.

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:47.580
LARS: Have you ever tried ice diving?
GORDON: I've never been ice diving.

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:49.300
I've done lots of diving, but...

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:54.460
LARS: It's a special kind of diving, and you need some special skills, but-- We will try it now.

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:58.640
GORDON: Don't make the hole too small. I want to get out easy, just in case those f***ing things are huge.

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:03.680
GORDON: Will we stay completely dry?
LARS: Hopefully, yeah.

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:05.600
GORDON: I've never dived in a dry suit before.

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:09.920
(WHISPERS) Bloody hell, shit.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:13.680
Oh f***. (LAUGHS) That's one leg.

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:21.120
Shh, god! I don't think there's any water getting in there, is there?

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:24.640
I feel like a big, f***ing condom!
LARS: At least you are very safe.

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:28.800
GORDON: Gor! Bloody hell. That's hard work, that. Huh?

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:34.080
VOICEOVER: Ice diving can be extremely dangerous,

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:37.520
as it is so easy to become disorientated in the freezing dark water.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:39.440
I'm shitting myself.

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:41.760
(BLOWS ON RE-BREATHER)

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:44.720
LARS: When you fetch a crab, you should just grab one of their legs.

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:49.280
The claws are very strong, so they can snap your finger, or even-- more--

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:51.680
GORDON: So if I'm swimming over one, watch out for my widger.

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:54.400
Should be cold down there, I don't want it snapped off.
(LAUGHING)

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:55.840
Okay...

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:01.440
F*** me, it's freezing!

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:05.280
(LAUGHING) Shit! My f***ing boots. Whew!

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:14.480
VOICEOVER: We could get hypothermia if we stay down here too long.

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:17.120
So we've got to be quick, but that's easier said than done.

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:20.560
I can see the crabs, but I cant' see the surface.

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:38.240
These freakish beasts grow up to six feet wide, and have no natural predators.

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:40.880
So it's down to us to bring their invasion under control.

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:11.360
GORDON: God!

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:12.560
Ah!

00:04:14.240 --> 00:04:15.680
God Almighty!

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:18.000
A lot harder than I thought it would be.

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:20.080
Look at the size of the thing!

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:21.680
And look at that!

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:24.000
Beautiful! (KISSES)

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:26.880
My balls feel like two big, f***ing ice cubes.

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:35.760
VOICEOVER: Lars has shown me how to catch a giant crab. Now I'm going to show him a new way to eat it.

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:38.080
But first, I've got to kill it.

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:46.000
LARS: Then its dead. (INAUDIBLE)

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:51.040
We cut off the legs and boil them in seawater for 15 minutes,

00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:53.840
discarding the body, which isn't that good to eat.

00:04:54.720 --> 00:04:59.920
GORDON: Because the quality of the King Crab is so delicious, it doesn't need much more.

00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:04.960
So I'm just going to do something very simple with creme fresh mayonnaise, and some tarragon,

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:06.560
and some lime, okay?

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:15.120
I'm making the sauce by mixing equal amounts of mayonnaise and creme fresh, with some lime zest,

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:16.880
salt and pepper,

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:20.560
roughly chopped tarragon, and freshly squeezed lime juice.

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:22.080
Delicious.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:24.560
GORDON: Nice.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:26.560
Lovely.

00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:30.560
LARS: You can try to break the main joint here, and if you're lucky--

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:33.680
GORDON: You'll keep it whole,
LARS: The meat will come out like this.

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:34.960
GORDON: Lovely.

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:37.920
It's the size of a lobster tail, isn't it?

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:41.200
Now look at that. That, smells and looks amazing.

00:05:41.680 --> 00:05:44.240
This... is what I've been waiting for.

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:49.520
GORDON: Beautiful!

00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:53.120
Mmm. That's delicious.

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:54.560
My god.

00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:56.720
LARS: I actually now think, I prefer it to lobster.

00:05:56.720 --> 00:05:59.200
GORDON: It's so much softer, and sweeter.

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:01.440
GORDON: Is there any more?

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:03.280
Or do I have to go back down, and get another one?

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:05.520
LARS: (LAUGHING) You have to go back down.

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:06.640
GORDON: F***ing hell...

